The consumable buffer revision from 6 to 9 months reflects the operational reality that an Earth-Mars synodic cycle—the window for potential external intervention, supply delivery, or IRB review—extends to approximately 26 months, and a 9-month buffer ensures survival through the communication and decision latency of any external review process. This revision is a direct operationalization of the Dependency Reduction Doctrine’s principle that sovereignty must be physically earned; until Mars achieves launch independence (Milestone 4, Year 15), Earth may retain a residual capacity to intervene in a PSM situation through supply or evacuation.

5.5 Sensory and Environmental Mediation Systems

The sensory environment of a sealed habitat is inherently monotonous. Recycled air has a constant chemical signature. Artificial lighting, if unchanging, disrupts circadian rhythms. The absence of natural soundscapes produces a background of mechanical hum that, over time, becomes a cognitive stressor. The Sensory and Environmental Mediation Systems are the technological instantiation of the Psychological Governance Mandate.

System Specification Governance Link
