Appendix B: The Dual Legitimacy Model — Domain Authority Rules

B.1 Domain Definition

A Technical Safety Domain is any operational area where:

· Erroneous action would result in probable death of multiple settlers within 30 days if unmitigated;
· The knowledge required for competent decision-making requires certification beyond general settler training.

The Facilitation Committee, upon advice from current Domain Holders, maintains a public list of Domains. Initial Domains: Reactor Operations, Atmospheric Management, Water Recycling, Medical Quarantine (biocontainment), Habitat Structural Integrity.

B.2 Certification and Deputies

· Certification examination is public and accessible to any settler.
· Peer review by existing Domain Holders assesses practical competence.
· The settlement must maintain ≥3 certified Domain Holders for each Domain (Bus Factor ≥3).
· No person may be the sole Domain Holder for any Domain for >6 consecutive months.

B.3 Binding Directive Protocol

A Domain Holder may issue a binding directive within their Domain. It must:

1. Be justified in writing with technical reasoning.
2. Be logged in the public Domain Authority Register.
3. Be automatically reviewed at the next Monthly Review.
4. May be overturned at that review by a 2/3 supermajority.

B.4 Boundary Disputes

The Facilitation Committee adjudicates whether a decision falls within a Domain or is a general governance matter. Its determination may be appealed to the full settlement by simple majority vote within 7 days.

