Appendix C: Palliative Separation Protocol — Full Operational Specification

C.1 Prerequisites

· Exhaustion of all restorative interventions, documented in SGN ledger.
· Individual has refused or failed to complete ≥2 Restorative Justice Circles.
· Pattern of behaviour established through Monthly Review records demonstrating persistent, severe threat to collective survival.
· 4/5 supermajority vote.

C.2 Voting Procedure

· Anonymous digital vote using SGN voting protocol.
· Ballot text states specific behaviours constituting the threat.
· Individual receives text 48 hours prior; may submit written response distributed to voters.

C.3 External Review

· Within 48 hours of invocation, case file transmitted to Independent Review Body (IRB).
· IRB composition: Earth ethics panel (initial), rotating inter-settlement panel (mature phase).
· IRB may request documents, interview individual via delayed text.
· IRB issues public, non-binding opinion. Finding of "unlawful" triggers mandatory settlement-wide revote.
· Second IRB finding of unlawful after confirming revote requires release.

C.4 PSM Conditions

· Individual relocated to PSM module (specifications: Appendix H).
· PSM Liaison appointed (rotated quarterly), not party to prior conflicts.
· Supplies delivered via pass-through airlock.
· Medical checks offered remotely; no forced entry except to prevent imminent death from module failure.
· Status reviewed every 6 months; reintegration requires individual request and simple majority vote.
· Settlement commits to indefinite care.

