Appendix D: Resource Partition Framework

Full specification as developed in Chapter 3, Section 3.4, reproduced here for reference.

Category A: Non-Divisible Infrastructure
Nuclear reactor, primary greenhouse, main habitat spine, central comms. Retained by originating settlement; departing group receives usage rights under 5-year treaty at pre-negotiated rates.

Category B: Divisible Consumables
Food, water, medical supplies, refined fuel. Proportional allocation based on departing population percentage, with 10% transition penalty to originating settlement.

Category C: Knowledge Commons
Genetic libraries, software codebases, research data, constitutional text. Non-exclusive, perpetual, royalty-free license to both parties.

Category D: Fabricated Assets
Rovers, spacesuits, tools, 3D printers, portable hab modules. Departing group selects items up to proportional share by verified valuation. Disputes resolved by alternating pick, originating settlement first.

Category E: Foundational Infrastructure
Landing pads, excavated tunnels, radiation shielding, water-ice mining sites. Originating settlement retains ownership; departing group receives 10-year lease at maintenance-cost pricing, renegotiable thereafter.

