Appendix E: Charter of Generational Rights (Constitutional Article VI, Full Text)

VI.1 Reproductive Sovereignty
No person may be compelled or prevented from reproducing, except: (a) where pregnancy would create probable, imminent death risk to the pregnant person, certified by Medical Officer and reviewed by Domain panel; (b) under validly invoked Article I emergency where supporting pregnancy/infancy would degrade life-support below CRI safety threshold.

VI.2 Child Sovereignty
A Mars-born person attains full participatory sovereignty at age 16 Martian years, or earlier by competence certification. Prior to this age, they possess: (a) bodily autonomy except for guardian-consented medical care; (b) right to be heard in all matters affecting them; (c) right to education in constitutional literacy, technical competence, and conflict resolution.

VI.3 Guardianship
Upon parental death or incapacitation, guardianship transfers to: (a) named guardian in pre-filed parental directive; (b) if none, Facilitation Committee appoints from volunteers, subject to child's age-weighted preference and settlement ratification by simple majority.

VI.4 Reproductive Medicine
Moratorium on heritable genetic modification until Reproductive Ethics Protocol drafted by third Annual Convention and ratified by 2/3 majority, except to prevent fatal genetic disease.

