Appendix L: Glossary of Key Terms

· Article I (Survival Imperative): The constrained principle that collective survival may temporarily override individual rights under procedurally bounded emergency powers.
· Constitutional Risk Index (CRI): Composite metric of life-support system health that governs emergency power invocation.
· Domain Authority: Certified technical expert empowered to issue binding safety directives, subject to democratic override.
· Dual Legitimacy Model: Governance structure separating political equality from technical Domain Authority.
· Facilitation Committee: Elected process stewards with no decision-making power.
· Palliative Separation Module (PSM): Dignified quarantine habitat for irrecoverable individuals threatening collective survival.
· Resource Partition Framework: Ex ante rules for dividing assets during secession.
· Settlement Governance Network (SGN): Air-gapped, cryptographically secured digital democracy infrastructure.
· Dependency Reduction Doctrine: Treaty mechanism for graduated sovereignty through measurable autonomy milestones.
· Anti-Capture Mechanisms: Rules preventing power concentration (rotation, lottery, cooling-off, COI registry, bus factor).
· Psychological Governance Mandates: Constitutional commitments to decompression, counseling, burnout protection, grief protocol, emotional leave, silence rights.

